/node_modules
dist/
.vite/
*.local

# Sketchfab API token. `scripts/fetch-assets.mjs` reads it from
# SKETCHFAB_API_TOKEN or from this file; it is a personal credential and must
# never be committed. See the Sketchfab section of ASSET_LICENSES.md.
sketchfab-token

# Research credentials (Firecrawl, Apify). Same rule as the Sketchfab token:
# personal, and nothing in the build reads them — they exist so a session can
# reach documentation that is behind a bot challenge. This entry is load-bearing
# rather than tidy: the workflow in this repository uses `git add -A`, so an
# unignored `.env` is one commit away from being published.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Playwright
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright-mcp/

# Verification-loop scratch output
local-*.png
diff-*.png
tests/__screenshots__/actual/

# Captures of the third-party reference site. Kept locally to drive the visual
# comparison loop, deliberately not redistributed in this repository.
reference/shots/

# Raw asset downloads for the scene dressing.
#
# `scripts/fetch-assets.mjs` pulls Poly Haven's and Sketchfab's film-quality
# source — 555 MB of it — and `scripts/optimize-assets.mjs` decimates and
# Meshopt-encodes that into `public/models/dressing/*.glb`, which is what ships
# and what is committed. Both steps are reproducible, so the source has no
# business in the history: keeping it would multiply the repository by fifteen to
# store geometry no frame draws.
#
# It lives outside `public/` for a second reason. Vite copies `public/` into
# `dist/` verbatim, so while these sat there the optimiser was being undone one
# directory up and the build shipped 818 MB. `public/models/` now holds only what
# a URL points at: the ship, the buoy, the barrel, the two silhouette rocks, and
# the `dressing/` outputs.
#
# Re-fetching the Sketchfab half needs a personal API token, so a contributor
# without one still gets a working build from the committed outputs.
assets/source/

# Scratch space for `scripts/modelkit/sketchfab.mjs get`, which lands a candidate
# here so `inspect`/`shells`/`plates` and the viewer can be pointed at it before
# anyone decides whether it is worth a manifest entry. Nothing here ships.
public/models/_preview/

# Reference material fetched for study, never for reuse. Shadertoy's default
# licence is CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 and two of the shaders in here are stricter still,
# so this must not enter the tree: doing so would relicense the project. See
# research/shadertoy/README.md, which records the terms and what was taken from
# each one as *technique*.
research/

# Scratch capture specs used for eyeballing tuning changes between tasks.
tests/_probe*.spec.ts

# Impeccable's design skill, installed with `npx impeccable install`. Six harness
# directories, each a full copy of the same ~150 files, because the installer
# targets every harness it finds on the machine rather than the one in use.
#
# Untracked rather than vendored: it is tooling for whoever is editing the UI,
# not part of what this project builds or ships, and its own guidance is that a
# team wanting it pinned should use the git-submodule install instead. The design
# decisions it produced are recorded in PRODUCT.md and DESIGN.md, which *are*
# tracked — those are the durable artefacts.
.agents/
.claude/
.codex/
.cursor/
.gemini/
.opencode/
.impeccable/config.local.json
.impeccable/hook.cache.json
.impeccable/*.png
.impeccable/live/sessions/
.impeccable/live/previews/
# Transcripts of the decision pages the skill serves while a direction is being
# chosen. The *outcome* is recorded in the direction contract at the top of
# index.html and in DESIGN.md; these are the scratch behind it.
.impeccable/questions/

# Scratch capture harness — drives a headless browser against its own preview
# server to screenshot the UI while a design change is being judged. Kept out of
# `scripts/` because nothing in the build or the suite calls it.
_shoot.mjs
.vite-cache/
